  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/379871096",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3544#issuecomment-379871096",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/3544",
    "id": 379871096,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3OTg3MTA5Ng==",
    "user": {
      "login": "bzbarsky",
      "id": 1457979,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTc5Nzk=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1457979?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bzbarsky",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bzbarsky/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2018-04-09T19:44:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-09T19:44:32Z",
    "body": "Note that the things that browsers delay for and the things that might lead to error instead of load may not be the same set.\r\n\r\nThat is, I expect even browsers that don't let non-toplevel imports make the load error out still wait for them before firing load...  Testcase:\r\n\r\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\r\n    <script>\r\n      var start = performance.now();\r\n    </script>\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\"\r\n          href=\"data:text/css,@import url(&quot;data:text/css,@import url('http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/cgi/test-tools/delayed-file?pause=4&mime=text%2Fhtml&text=NOT+A+STYLESHEET');&quot;)\"\r\n          onload=\"alert('loaded in: ' + (performance.now() - start))\"\r\n          onerror=\"alert('errored in: ' + (performance.now() - start))\">\r\n\r\nand that shows \"loaded in\" followed by a 4+s time in Chrome.  So it's waiting for that innermost import, but then ignoring that it failed.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/379871096/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
