    "created_at": "2018-04-09T21:16:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-09T21:16:12Z",
    "body": "It's amazing what you can inline into a single-file test case...\r\n\r\nTo me a reasonable model would be that error events only fire if the top-level sheet itself fails to come over the network. Any ideas if that is consistent with browsers at all? (I can write tests if you haven't already.) It's certainly not allowed by the current spec, which says that if any critical subresource fails, you must fire error and must not fire load.\r\n\r\nIt does seem like this whole area needs a more comprehensive test suite. I guess I'm up for taking over that enterprise. You have some tests already written, right? Can you point me to them?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/379896671/reactions",
